\section{Amending provisions}{


Danish amending instruments (\verb{BEK Æ}, \verb{LOV Æ}, \code{ANG}) contain \code{Paragraf}
elements that are \strong{not their own}: they are new text to be inserted into
another instrument, nested under \code{AendringNyTekst}. An amending regulation
may therefore appear to have sections that in fact belong to the act it
amends.

The \code{is_amendment} column distinguishes the two. In a consolidated act it
is \code{FALSE} throughout; in an amending instrument it is typically \code{TRUE}
throughout. Filter on it before treating the output as the document's own
structure.
}

\section{Known limitation}{


